{
  "analysis": "We have installed primer3 (oligotm) and identified exact sequence boundaries. The output plasmid consists of: input[0..209] | egfp[0..713] (excluding TAA stop) | flag[3..86] (excluding ATG start and TAA stop) | snap[3..548] (excluding ATG start) | input[687..end]. Now I need to extract the exact 4-nt overhangs at each junction and design primers with BsaI tails.",
  "plan": "Run a Perl script to extract the exact 4-nt Golden Gate overhangs at each of the 4 junctions. Then design primer annealing regions, add BsaI tails (GGTCTC + 4nt overhang), validate Tms with oligotm, and write primers.fasta.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "perl - <<'PERL'
use strict; use warnings;
my %s;my $n;
open my $F,'<','sequences.fasta' or die $!;
while(<$F>){chomp; if(/^>(\S+)/){$n=$1} else {$s{$n}.=uc($_)}}

# Junction coordinates (0-based, end-exclusive)
# Junction 1: input[0..209] | output[210..]  => overhang = output[206..210)
# Junction 2: output[923] | output[924..]   => overhang = output[920..924)
# Junction 3: output[1007] | output[1008..] => overhang = output[1004..1008)
# Junction 4: output[1550] | output[1551..] => overhang = output[1547..1551)
print "O1 (input->egfp): ",substr($s{output},206,4),"\n";
print "O2 (egfp->flag): ",substr($s{output},920,4),"\n";
print "O3 (flag->snap): ",substr($s{output},1004,4),"\n";
print "O4 (snap->input): ",substr($s{output},1547,4),"\n";

# Context around each junction
print "\nContext:\n";
for my $p (210, 924, 1008, 1551){
  print "J at $p: ",substr($s{output},$p-8,16)," | mark at $p=",substr($s{output},$p,1),"\n";
}

# Print full output around each junction
print "\nJ1 context: ",substr($s{output},196,28),"\n";
print "J2 context: ",substr($s{output},910,28),"\n";
print "J3 context: ",substr($s{output},994,28),"\n";
print "J4 context: ",substr($s{output},1540,28),"\n";
PERL
",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
 "task_complete": false
}
